ic ships only a stale_claim inbox notification for ops-alert tickets (flag-only, 4h, no auto-release). Research conclusions to carry: every incident tool answers 'acknowledger vanished' (PagerDuty ack timeout re-triggers, Icinga ack expiry, k8s Lease renew); rebar's claim is an un-timed soft lock with no inverse op (release = transition back to open). Critique verdict: auto-release and heartbeats are wrong for LLM sessions (review-plan 15-20 min, make verify 25 min, /rebar-implement hours are legitimately silent; heartbeats amplify commit rate on the tickets branch). Recommended shape: an explicit release op (the honest inverse of claim) plus flag-only staleness at 24h for general tickets.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"idea","tags":[],"ticket_id":"dc36-bad6-b303-4a20","ticket_type":"epic","title":"Explicit claim release/yield op + stale-claim policy for time-sensitive tickets","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b928cb06-7f0f-45d2-b4f0-6bd407a959a0","a477c0d5-d1d4-41af-99ac-ea06a374f236"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788568426448701212,"uuid":"42612567-33a8-4c59-a86f-6cb8ddd19892"}